KG42.register("clusters-7ff52c1d344a0254e5062be7",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v142-d-CL004","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","label":"Calculation of period bills according to system surplus or deficit and individual deviation contributions","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL004","label":"Calculation of period bills according to system surplus or deficit and individual deviation contributions","market_meaning":"Individual and group deviations are calculated from planned and actual net energy. Combining the system's actual surplus or deficit, prosumer roles, and the directions of individual deviations, MGO applies the corresponding billing branches and contribution-adjustment criteria.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"This covers only M02 deviation billing for each period. Eq. (9) distinguishes roles according to planned net energy, and all eight billing conditions are retained separately; penalty-free amounts of the same form occur under different system conditions and cannot be deduplicated. Planned and actual quantities remain distinct, while zero deviation, role reversal, and the profit baseline across surplus and deficit regions remain unresolved.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This single chain already contains deviation inputs, aggregate determinations, and bill outputs, and has independent settlement significance. It maintains mechanism boundaries with the base utility monetary terms in M01 and benchmark pricing in M03; object identity is not inferred from price or payment nodes sharing the same name.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R011","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Jointly retains the deviation definitions, aggregate conditions, eight billing branches, and individual contribution criteria as a single deviation-billing candidate."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The billing branches list only strictly positive and strictly negative individual deviations, without specifying provisions applicable to zero deviation. When the net energy of a seller or buyer classified according to the plan reverses in actual operation, it is also unclear whether reclassification occurs and how billing is performed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::delta_n_hourly_deviation","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C010","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C001","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C005","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e026","v141-b-g01-e027","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g01-e033"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must clarify the scope of applicability for zero deviation, planned zero net energy, and actual role reversal; payment rules from other mechanisms must not be borrowed automatically to fill these gaps."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The contribution criterion depends on a comparison of actual and planned profits, but Eqs. (12)/(17) expand the baseline terms using the electricity price for the actual surplus or deficit region. When the plan and actual operation fall in different surplus or deficit regions, it is not explained whether this baseline still equals the original planned profit; R^o also lacks complete typing and definition in this chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C009","v141-c-R011::theta::E_s_total_selling_energy","v141-c-R011::theta::E_b_total_buying_energy","v141-c-R011::x::delta_b_total_deviation","v141-c-R011::x::delta_s_total_deviation"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e030","v141-b-g02-E22"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the baseline branch for planned profit and the treatment of deviations across regions, recheck whether contribution determination requires additional conditions, and then have C supply the required objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G003","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"For sellers, B_n represents revenue, whereas for buyers, B_n represents payment; these cannot be merged under a uniform cash-flow direction. The text near source Eq. (15) says \"selling energy\", whereas the formula concerns a buyer quantity; the penalty coefficients in Eqs. (16)/(19) also differ from those used in the corresponding profit-contribution expressions, so exact compensation for MGO losses cannot be claimed directly.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::B_n_bill","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C002","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C006","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C007","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g01-e029","v141-b-g01-e030","v141-b-g01-e032"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the direction of bill flows, textual discrepancies, and the design rationale for the penalty coefficients; retain the original expressions, and do not derive an unspecified compensation equality from the sign of the contribution."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G004","category":"upstream_missing","description":"B provides Eqs. (22)-(23) for updating MGO profit according to the final bills, but the existing C chain lacks the corresponding profit objects and constraints. Individual billing branches can therefore currently be displayed, but closure of the complete settlement revenue and expenditure accounts cannot yet be checked.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R011::x::B_n_bill","v141-c-R011::phi::v141-c-R011-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g01-e036"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"To form a complete settlement-accounting rule, C must supplement bill aggregation and the representation of MGO's final profit; D does not directly add formulas from B that were omitted from the catalog."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G005","category":"unverified_source","description":"All evidence underlying bills and deviations retains UNREVIEWED/unverified status; this experiment has not independently checked transcription or the scientific interpretation of bills.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R011"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e023","v141-b-g01-e024","v141-b-g01-e025","v141-b-g01-e026","v141-b-g01-e027","v141-b-g01-e028","v141-b-g01-e029","v141-b-g01-e030","v141-b-g01-e031","v141-b-g01-e032","v141-b-g01-e033","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g03-E19"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the source conditions, deviation definitions, and bill amounts branch by branch, and subsequently examine the mathematical interpretations independently."}]},"rule_refs":["14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R011"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2ad9b5ceb5b441cd","COMP-8e34b40deae71479"]});
